 ("Can I import a 3D printer from China to Pakistan?", "Yes. One printer for your own use can be imported like other machinery. Check the voltage version, avoid units marked for mainland China only, and budget for shipping on the box size, not the printer weight."),
 ("Do Bambu Lab printers work on 220V in Pakistan?", "The A1 mini and P1S list 100 to 240 VAC. Newer models such as the P2S and H2D are sold in separate voltage versions, so ask the seller for the 220 to 240V unit."),
 ("What is the Bambu Lab China region lock?", "Owners on Bambu's forum report that printers sold for mainland China can only bind to Bambu's China cloud, which limits app use and updates elsewhere. Ask for the global version in writing."),
 ("Is it cheaper to import 3D printer parts than a full printer?", "Much cheaper to ship. An A1 series hotend heating assembly ships in a 40 g pack, while a boxed printer is charged as 13 to 44 kg depending on the model."),
 ("Should I import filament from China?", "Usually not on its own. A 1 kg spool is cheap and heavy, so shipping often costs more than the filament. It can make sense added to a printer order or for a rare material."),
